title: Veeam: Protection Groups
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors an agent protection group of a Veeam Backup & Replication
 server, collected via the Veeam special agent. Reading protection groups
 requires the Veeam Backup Administrator or Restore Operator role.

 The summary shows the following values:

 Type: how the group selects its computers: "Individual computers",
 "Manually added", "Unmanaged", "Active Directory objects", "CSV file",
 "Pre-installed agents", "Cloud machines" or "MongoDB".

 Configured computers: the number of computers listed in the group's
 configuration, not the number discovered or backed up. Only groups of type
 "Individual computers" and "Manually added" list their computers; for all
 other types the count is left out of the summary, and the details say so.

 State: whether the group is "Enabled" or "Disabled".

 The details show the group's description.

 This check is {OK} by default if the protection group is disabled; the
 state is configurable, since a deliberately disabled protection group is
 normal in some estates. Otherwise it is {OK}.

discovery:
 One service is created for each agent protection group reported by the API.

item:
 The name of the protection group.
